To avoid overfitting and the "curse of dimensionality," our methodology does not assume a static lag structure across the forecasting horizon. Instead, at every rolling quarter, the model dynamically searches the parameter space to identify the optimal lag lengths (p and q_j) using the Bayesian Information Criterion (BIC). The BIC heavily penalizes model complexity:
