Algorithmic Tuning and Real-Time Nowcasting
The tuning parameter \lambda dictates the severity of the penalty. In our methodology, \lambda is dynamically optimized using k-fold Cross-Validation (CV) at every rolling window to find the exact floor of the out-of-sample forecasting error. As \lambda increases, the algorithm forces the coefficients of weaker, noisy indicators exactly to zero, performing simultaneous variable selection and regularization.
The resulting LASSO-MIDAS architecture provides a highly reactive nowcasting engine. It continuously ingests asynchronous monthly data releases, filters out the macroeconomic noise, and updates the quarterly GDP prediction in real-time, providing policymakers with an accurate, high-fidelity signal well ahead of official statistical publications.
